Z||000000||FieroMaster88||11-28-2000||01:31 AM||||Hello,<P>I just got a 1984 Indy Fiero for $500.  It runs and drives like new.  The engine has 135,000 miles on it and only needs minor work (a tune up) and a detail.  The frame and suspension is rust free.  The interior is trashed.  Both seats have rips in them and the back window has 5 nice bulllet holes from a pellet gun.  The steering column has about 3" of play in it in any direction. The front facia needs replacing, it is cracked, and the car needs a paint job.  The rims also need to be refinished.  But all in all i love the car.  It will go well with my 88 coupe.<P>Does anyone have any idea on where I can get parts to restore it, mainly the seat covers and other stuff.  The cheaper the better.<P>Thanks,<P>James||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||11-28-2000||08:00 AM||||Bob Stieger at Twin Lakes Fiero had several Pace car parts car at his shop. <A HREF="http://twinlakesfiero.tripod.com" TARGET=_blank>http://twinlakesfiero.tripod.com</A>   Original equipment replacement seats may be difficult, but you could get some specialty seats from Mr. Mike.||||reg||3
